      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree about adding acceleration to movement. I've been using holoporting for months, and have recently tried to acclimate myself to free movement, but the jarring nature of it instantly accelerating you puts me off and makes me want to go back to holoporting again. I don't know if they decided to go this way because of early VR research that suggested moving the player at a constant speed was less likely to make them sick, or what, but for me personally, even though free movement in VRChat makes me ill sometimes, I found playing Tsumuri Kart wasn't that bad. Perhaps the untextured roadways help as I have found I get less sick in worlds where the floor isn't detailed, but I flew around the track for a good half an hour and spun out repeatedly and only felt slightly nauseous by the end. So I suspect that I would handle movement with acceleration as well if not better than instant acceleration.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
