      "value": "@{5c75107d0678a11a9b404cd1|full_name}: I think it was based off of how you only ever feel acceleration and seeing acceleration but not feeling it is the thing that makes one sick, but the research on the effects of VR on people remains to be studied further since it had only just recently reached a consumer level (relatively, $499 is a lot cheaper than $20,000~40,000). Anyways you can actually control your speed with advanced control modes turned on but it makes it almost impossible to control your gestures and things.\n\nI really would rather just have a control config menu.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
