      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c8f538975056470640f1d9f|full_name}: Stutter-stepping refers to a means of flying by cheating gravity. If you have free movement turned on (as opposed to holoporting) you can jump off a cliff and repeatedly tap forward on the joystick to, in essence, glide to distant locations you might not otherwise be able to reach. This tapping is called \"stutter stepping\" because you move forward in a jerky manner when you tap the stick.\n\nSo what this person is suggesting is that flying by stutter-stepping be removed because they feel it breaks immersion. But also the broken physics that allow it result in people getting stuck on walls if they touch them when going down ramps.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
